.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]NMS_Tools\f[R] is a unified collection of deterministic,
audit\[u2011]transparent monitoring and inspection utilities used across
Linktech Engineering infrastructure.
Each tool follows strict engineering principles:
.IP \[bu] 2
Predictable, reproducible behavior
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \[bu] 2
No hidden state
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \[bu] 2
Audit\[u2011]transparent output
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \[bu] 2
Strict separation between human and machine modes
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \[bu] 2
Minimal dependencies
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \[bu] 2
Monitoring\[u2011]friendly design
.PP
The suite provides consistent CLI patterns, JSON schemas, logging
behavior, and operational semantics across all included tools.
.SH INCLUDED TOOLS
.SS check_ports.py \[em] Deterministic Multi\[u2011]Port TCP Checker
.PP
\f[V]check_ports.py\f[R] performs deterministic TCP availability checks
against one or more ports on a target host.
It supports explicit ports (\f[V]-p\f[R]) and service names
(\f[V]-s\f[R]), resolving services through the system\[cq]s service
database (e.g., \f[V]/etc/services\f[R]).
.PP
The tool provides: - Deterministic open / closed / timeout / unreachable
evaluation - Single\[u2011]service and single\[u2011]port
Nagios\[u2011]grade output - Multi\[u2011]port Nagios output for
monitoring systems - Verbose mode with full resolution context - JSON
mode for automation pipelines - Optional operator\[u2011]grade logging
with START / PORT / RESULT / END banners
.PP
Typical usage: \f[V]check_ports.py -H host -s ssh\f[R]
\f[V]check_ports.py -H host -p 443\f[R]
\f[V]check_ports.py -H host -s https,ssh -p 2222\f[R]
.PP
See \f[B]check_ports(1)\f[R] for full documentation.
.SS check_weather.py \[em] Deterministic Weather Condition Evaluator
.PP
check_weather.py evaluates current weather conditions using a
deterministic rule engine and a provider registry.
It is designed for automation workflows that depend on environmental
state (e.g., wind thresholds, precipitation detection).
.PP
The tool provides:
.IP \[bu] 2
Deterministic evaluation of temperature, wind, precipitation, and
visibility
.IP \[bu] 2
Provider registry with pluggable backends (Open\[u2011]Meteo, NOAA,
etc.)
.IP \[bu] 2
JSON and verbose output modes
.IP \[bu] 2
Rule\[u2011]based condition evaluation (e.g., \[lq]unsafe\[rq],
\[lq]advisory\[rq], \[lq]clear\[rq])
.IP \[bu] 2
Optional operator\[u2011]grade logging
.PP
Typical usage:
.PP
\f[V]check_weather.py --location \[dq]St John, KS\[dq]\f[R]
\f[V]check_weather.py --location 67576 --json\f[R]
.PP
See \f[B]check_weather(1)\f[R] for full documentation.
.SS check_cert.py \[em] TLS Certificate Inspection and Policy Enforcement
.PP
check_cert.py performs deterministic TLS certificate inspection and
policy evaluation.
It extracts certificate metadata, validates chains, and enforces
expiration and signature policies.
.PP
The tool provides:
.IP \[bu] 2
Deterministic JSON metadata extraction
.IP \[bu] 2
Expiration, SAN, issuer, and signature algorithm evaluation
.IP \[bu] 2
AIA chain reconstruction
.IP \[bu] 2
OCSP metadata extraction
.IP \[bu] 2
Policy enforcement with Nagios\[u2011]grade exit codes
.IP \[bu] 2
Clean separation between human and machine output modes
.PP
Typical usage:
.PP
\f[V]check_cert.py -H example.com\f[R]
\f[V]check_cert.py -H api.example.com --json\f[R]
.PP
See \f[B]check_cert(1)\f[R] for full documentation.
.SS check_html.py \[em] HTTP/HTTPS Inspection and Content Validation
.PP
check_html.py performs deterministic HTTP/HTTPS inspection with
content\[u2011]type, status\[u2011]code, and backend validation.
It is designed for monitoring web services and enforcing expected
response characteristics.
.PP
The tool provides:
.IP \[bu] 2
TLS\[u2011]aware request pipeline with handshake detection
.IP \[bu] 2
Status, headers, content\[u2011]type, and HTML body capture
.IP \[bu] 2
Backend fingerprinting and backend enforcement
.IP \[bu] 2
Deterministic JSON schema for automation
.IP \[bu] 2
Nagios\[u2011]aware severity merging (CRITICAL > WARNING > UNKNOWN > OK)
.PP
Typical usage:
.PP
\f[V]check_html.py -H example.com\f[R]
\f[V]check_html.py -H example.com --expect-backend nginx\f[R]
.PP
See \f[B]check_html(1)\f[R] for full documentation.
.SS check_interfaces.py \[em] Network Interface and SNMP Operational State Checker
.PP
check_interfaces.py evaluates network interface state using SNMP and
local system inspection.
It is designed for deterministic monitoring of link status,
administrative state, and operational counters.
.PP
The tool provides:
.IP \[bu] 2
SNMP\[u2011]based interface enumeration and state evaluation
.IP \[bu] 2
Deterministic admin/oper status mapping
.IP \[bu] 2
Optional local interface inspection (Linux)
.IP \[bu] 2
JSON and verbose output modes
.IP \[bu] 2
Operator\[u2011]grade logging with START/RESULT/END lifecycle
.PP
Typical usage:
.PP
\f[V]check_interfaces.py -H switch01\f[R]
\f[V]check_interfaces.py -H router01 --json\f[R]
.PP
See \f[B]check_interfaces(1)\f[R] for full documentation.
.SH DIRECTORY STRUCTURE
.PP
A typical installation includes:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
/usr/local/bin/              Executables
/usr/local/share/man/man1/   Tool man pages
/usr/local/share/man/man7/   Suite overview (this page)
/var/log/nms_tools/          Optional logging directory
\f[R]
.fi
.SH LOGGING
.PP
Tools may emit operator\[u2011]grade logs with rotation when configured
via:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
--log-dir <path>
--log-max-mb <size>
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Logging is deterministic and free of noise, suitable for automation and
post\[u2011]incident analysis.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
.PP
All tools support deterministic JSON output for automation pipelines.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Schemas are versioned and documented in:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
docs/Metadata_Schema.md
\f[R]
.fi
